      "content": "That sounds a lot more professional, but I'm still nervous. The gala presentation includes a slide that will show a map of the region with \"impacted areas\" highlighted. \n\nIf I show a map where only a tiny corner is highlighted, it's going to look like a failure, no matter how good the wording is. But if I highlight the whole region to show \"momentum,\" it might look like we're overstating things if someone actually checks the data later. \n\nDo you think we can just describe the progress as \"widely distributed across the target zone\" or something like that? I need the language to be strong enough that they don't question the actual numbers on that map. We can't afford any hesitation from them.",
